PROJECT GOAL & BEST PRACTICES (LLM BRIEF)

WHAT I’M BUILDING
- A web-based image generator:
  - Frontend: React + Vite UI
  - Backend: Node/Express API
  - Provider: Infip Images API (https://api.infip.pro/v1/images/generations)
- Primary use cases: all styles (photo, illustration, product, cinematic)
- Special requirements: consistent identity + high text-in-image accuracy

CORE REQUIREMENTS (MUST-HAVES)
1) API-only (no self-hosted GPU)
2) Return 1 final image to the user (for now)
3) Text in image must be accurate (logos, posters, labels, signage)
4) Identity consistency: same character/person should look consistent across generations

CONSTRAINTS & REALITIES
- Even strong models sometimes misspell or distort text.
- Consistent identity is hard with pure text-to-image unless:
  - reference images (img2img / guidance) are supported, or
  - editing workflow exists, or
  - post-processing is used for typography.

RECOMMENDED APPROACH (BEST-PRACTICE PIPELINE)

A) PROMPT FORMATTING / REFINEMENT (CRITICAL)
- Convert user input into structured fields:
  - subject, environment, style, composition, lighting, camera/medium, mood, color palette, constraints
- If user includes text, extract:
  - exact_text (must match exactly)
  - placement (top center / signboard / label area)
  - font_style (sans / serif / handwritten / brand-like)
  - contrast (dark text on light background, etc.)
- If we will overlay text ourselves:
  - instruct the model to “leave space for text”
  - instruct the model to NOT include any letters/words

B) GENERATE IMAGE
- Prefer Infip free models in this order:
  - default: img4 (fallback to img3)
  - optional: sdxl / flux variants / qwen depending on style needs
- Pass consistent parameters when supported:
  - seed, size/aspect ratio, quality, n

C) ENFORCE TEXT ACCURACY (RECOMMENDED)
For guaranteed correctness:
- Generate the image WITHOUT embedded text (or with a blank text area).
- Programmatically overlay the exact text server-side (Sharp/Canvas).
This ensures 100% spelling accuracy.

D) IDENTITY CONSISTENCY
- If provider supports reference guidance:
  - accept a reference image upload and pass it to the API (img2img / reference)
- If provider does NOT support identity locking:
  - use a “character sheet prompt” template:
  - stable physical description, stable outfit, stable framing, stable style keywords
  - reuse seed when supported
  - optional: generate 2 candidates internally, pick best, still return 1 to user

E) QUALITY CONTROLS
- Add guardrails:
  - reject empty prompts, normalize aspect ratio/size, limit prompt length
- Add retry logic for provider errors/timeouts

PROMPT TEMPLATES (COPY/PASTE)

